<div class="comparison-note">
  <p><strong>Documentation costs scale &mdash; toke's don't.</strong> With best practices applied, Python doubles from 41 &rarr; 82 tokens and Java grows from 62 &rarr; 102. toke stays at 24. In real codebases where every function carries docstrings, the gap compounds with every function added.</p>
</div>

<!-- ================================================================== -->
<!-- Why This Matters                                                   -->
<!-- ================================================================== -->

<div class="section-heading">
  <h2>Why This Matters</h2>
</div>

<div class="features">
  <div class="feature-card">
    <h3>40&ndash;75% Fewer Tokens</h3>
    <p>With toke's purpose-built BPE tokenizer, a complete fibonacci program uses 24 tokens &mdash; compared to 41 in Python, 52 in C, and 55 in Java (all cl100k_base). That is a 42% reduction vs Python and 56% vs Java. Add documentation and the gap widens further: Python doubles to 82 tokens and Java grows to 102, while toke stays at 24 because toke has no comment syntax &mdash; documentation lives in companion files. <a href="/tokenizer" style="color:#c792ea;">Try the live tokenizer &rarr;</a></p>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-card">
    <h3>Designed for Correctness</h3>
    <p>LL(1) grammar, 13 keywords, minimal character set (55 characters). No ambiguity, no implicit coercions, full static type checking. The compiler catches mistakes before code runs &mdash; critical when AI is writing the code.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-card">
    <h3>Standard Library with C Runtime</h3>
    <p>30+ standard library modules with C runtime implementations &mdash; strings, files, JSON, HTTP server, database, crypto, encoding, encryption, JWT auth, WebSocket, SSE, routing, templates, CSV, math, LLM integration, charting, dashboards, and machine learning. Common operations become single function calls.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-card">
    <h3>Open Source</h3>
    <p>MIT and Apache 2.0 licensed. Built in public. Every component &mdash; <a href="https://github.com/karwalski/toke">compiler</a>, <a href="https://github.com/karwalski/toke">spec</a>, <a href="https://github.com/karwalski/toke-model">corpus &amp; tokenizer</a>, <a href="https://github.com/karwalski/toke-eval">benchmarks</a>, <a href="https://github.com/karwalski/toke-web">docs</a>, <a href="https://github.com/karwalski/toke-mcp">MCP server</a> &mdash; is open for contribution and enterprise use.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ================================================================== -->
<!-- Quick Example                                                      -->
<!-- ================================================================== -->

<div class="section-heading">
  <h2>Quick Example</h2>
</div>

<div class="code-window" style="max-width:660px;margin:1rem auto 0.75rem;">
  <div class="titlebar"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
  <pre><span class="kw">m</span>=hello;
<span class="kw">i</span>=io:std.io;

<span class="kw">f</span>=<span class="fn">main</span>():<span class="kw">i64</span>{
  io.<span class="fn">println</span>(<span class="str">"Hello, world!"</span>);
  <span class="kw">&lt;</span><span class="num">0</span>;
};</pre>
</div>
<p class="section-desc">A complete toke program. <code style="background:#161616;border:1px solid #222;border-radius:3px;padding:0.15em 0.35em;font-size:0.82em;color:#c792ea;">m=</code> declares the module. <code style="background:#161616;border:1px solid #222;border-radius:3px;padding:0.15em 0.35em;font-size:0.82em;color:#c792ea;">i=</code> imports a library. <code style="background:#161616;border:1px solid #222;border-radius:3px;padding:0.15em 0.35em;font-size:0.82em;color:#c792ea;">f=</code> declares a function. <code style="background:#161616;border:1px solid #222;border-radius:3px;padding:0.15em 0.35em;font-size:0.82em;color:#c792ea;">&lt;</code> returns a value. Every statement ends with <code style="background:#161616;border:1px solid #222;border-radius:3px;padding:0.15em 0.35em;font-size:0.82em;color:#c792ea;">;</code>. No boilerplate, no ceremony.</p>

<!-- ================================================================== -->
<!-- Development Timeline                                               -->
<!-- ================================================================== -->

<div class="section-heading">
  <h2>Development Timeline</h2>
</div>

<div class="dev-timeline">

  <!-- PHASE 1 -->
  <div class="timeline-phase-group">
    <div class="phase-group-header">
      <span class="phase-group-label">Phase 1 (legacy 80-character syntax)</span>
      <span class="phase-group-title">Can AI write toke?</span>
    </div>
    <p class="phase-summary">The first phase answers a simple question: can existing AI models write valid toke programs, and does toke actually use fewer tokens than conventional languages? Everything built here is designed to prove &mdash; or disprove &mdash; the core thesis before investing further.</p>
    <p class="phase-technical">Epics 1.1&ndash;1.10. Gate 1 criteria: &gt;10% token reduction vs Python/C/Java (cl100k_base) AND Pass@1 &ge; 60% on held-out benchmark.</p>

    <div class="timeline-milestone complete">
      <div class="milestone-marker"></div>
      <div class="milestone-content">
        <div class="milestone-header">
          <span class="milestone-id">1.1</span>
          <span class="milestone-title">Language Specification</span>
          <span class="phase-status complete">Complete</span>
        </div>
        <p class="milestone-desc">Defined the complete toke language &mdash; grammar, keywords, types, operators, and the character sets for both profiles.</p>
        <p class="milestone-technical">LL(1) grammar, 13 keywords. Phase 1 (80 chars) for corpus generation. Phase 2 (55 chars) production encoding with <code>$</code> type sigils and <code>@()</code> arrays. Formal EBNF, RFC draft, mechanical transformation rules. <a href="https://github.com/karwalski/toke">toke</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="timeline-milestone complete">
      <div class="milestone-marker"></div>
      <div class="milestone-content">
        <div class="milestone-header">
          <span class="milestone-id">1.2</span>
          <span class="milestone-title">Reference Compiler</span>
          <span class="phase-status complete">Complete</span>
        </div>
        <p class="milestone-desc">Built the compiler that checks every toke program for correctness &mdash; type safety, syntax validity, and character set compliance.</p>
        <p class="milestone-technical">Single-pass C99 compiler: lexer, LL(1) parser, name resolution, type inference, LLVM IR codegen (x86-64, ARM64). <code>--check</code> mode for corpus validation. Structured JSON diagnostics. 600+ conformance tests. <a href="https://github.com/karwalski/toke">toke</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="timeline-milestone complete">
      <div class="milestone-marker"></div>
      <div class="milestone-content">
        <div class="milestone-header">
          <span class="milestone-id">1.3&ndash;1.9</span>
          <span class="milestone-title">Standard Library, Security &amp; Infrastructure</span>
          <span class="phase-status complete">Complete</span>
        </div>
        <p class="milestone-desc">6 core library modules (<code>std.str</code>, <code>std.http</code>, <code>std.db</code>, <code>std.json</code>, <code>std.file</code>, <code>std.net</code>), SAST analysis and fuzzing, corpus pipeline threat model, and monitoring dashboard.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="timeline-milestone complete">
      <div class="milestone-marker"></div>
      <div class="milestone-content">
        <div class="milestone-header">
          <span class="milestone-id">1.5</span>
          <span class="milestone-title">Training Corpus</span>
          <span class="phase-status complete">Complete</span>
        </div>
        <p class="milestone-desc">Built a library of 46,754 verified toke programs using three AI models in parallel (Haiku 4.5, GPT-4.1-mini, Grok-3-mini), each validated by the compiler and cross-checked against reference implementations in Python, C, and Java.</p>
        <p class="milestone-technical">339 task templates, 50K generated tasks. 4 corpus stages: 26,978 single-function (Stage A), 9,776 multi-function (Stage B), 5,000 edge cases (Stage C), 5,000 application-level (Stage D). Auto-fixer rescues ~15% of programs at zero API cost. <a href="https://github.com/karwalski/toke-model">toke-model</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="timeline-milestone complete">
      <div class="milestone-marker"></div>
      <div class="milestone-content">
        <div class="milestone-header">
          <span class="milestone-id">1.6</span>
          <span class="milestone-title">Gate 1 Evaluation</span>
          <span class="phase-status complete">Complete</span>
        </div>
        <p class="milestone-desc">Final benchmark on 1,000 held-out tasks. <strong>Gate 1: PASS.</strong> Token reduction 12.5% (target &gt;10%). Pass@1 63.7% (target &ge;60%). Compilation rate 92.3%.</p>
        <p class="milestone-technical">1,000 held-out tasks, 120 test inputs each. Token reduction: 12.5% (8K vocab) / 13.1% (32K vocab) vs cl100k_base. Pass@1: 588/923 compilable tasks (63.7%) via Qwen 2.5 Coder 7B + QLoRA adapter. <a href="https://github.com/karwalski/toke-eval">toke-eval</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="gate-marker">
      <div class="gate-line"></div>
      <div class="gate-content">
        <span class="gate-label">Gate 1 &mdash; PASS</span>
        <span class="gate-criteria">&gt;10% token reduction AND Pass@1 &ge; 60%</span>
      </div>
      <div class="gate-line"></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- PHASE 2 -->
  <div class="timeline-phase-group">
    <div class="phase-group-header">
      <span class="phase-group-label">Phase 2 (default 55-character syntax)</span>
      <span class="phase-group-title">Custom tokenizer &amp; first AI model</span>
    </div>
    <p class="phase-summary">With the thesis validated, Phase 2 builds a tokenizer purpose-built for toke, expands the standard library, and works toward training a model on the production default syntax. A major syntax decision &mdash; adopting the 55-character encoding as the default &mdash; required regenerating the entire corpus in the new format.</p>
    <p class="phase-technical">Epics 2.1&ndash;2.5. Profile 2 (55-char) BPE tokenizer. QLoRA fine-tuning of Qwen 2.5 Coder 7B. Gate 2 criteria: 7B model outperforms baseline on default-syntax generation.</p>

    <div class="timeline-milestone complete">
      <div class="milestone-marker"></div>
      <div class="milestone-content">
        <div class="milestone-header">
          <span class="milestone-id">2.1</span>
          <span class="milestone-title">Language Extensions &amp; Default Syntax</span>
          <span class="phase-status complete">Complete</span>
        </div>
        <p class="milestone-desc">Adopted the 55-character encoding as the default (&ldquo;toke&rdquo;) and the 80-character encoding as the legacy profile (<code>--legacy</code>). Expanded the standard library to 30+ modules covering security, networking, data processing, visualization, and LLM integration.</p>
        <p class="milestone-technical">55-char is default, <code>$</code> type sigils, <code>@()</code> arrays, <code>[]</code> removed. 30+ stdlib modules with <code>.tki</code> interface contracts. <a href="https://github.com/karwalski/toke">toke</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="timeline-milestone complete">
      <div class="milestone-marker"></div>
      <div class="milestone-content">
        <div class="milestone-header">
          <span class="milestone-id">2.2</span>
          <span class="milestone-title">Purpose-Built Tokenizer</span>
          <span class="phase-status complete">Complete</span>
        </div>
        <p class="milestone-desc">BPE tokenizer retrained on the 25,953-record default-syntax corpus. 8,192 token vocabulary optimised for v0.3 patterns like <code>m=</code>, <code>f=</code>, <code>:i64):i64{</code>, and <code>&lt;0};</code>.</p>
        <p class="milestone-technical">8K BPE on 25,953 v0.3 programs. Phase 2 result: trained and deployed. Phase 1 legacy: 13.1% token reduction (32K vocab). <a href="https://github.com/karwalski/toke-model">toke-model</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="timeline-milestone complete">
      <div class="milestone-marker"></div>
      <div class="milestone-content">
        <div class="milestone-header">
          <span class="milestone-id">2.3</span>
          <span class="milestone-title">First Fine-Tuned Model (Gate 1)</span>
          <span class="phase-status complete">Complete</span>
        </div>
        <p class="milestone-desc">QLoRA fine-tune of Qwen 2.5 Coder 7B on the v0.3 default-syntax corpus. 25,953 training examples with canonical system prompt. Training in progress.</p>
        <p class="milestone-technical">QLoRA rank 64, alpha 128, cosine schedule. ChatML format with v0.3 canonical prompt. Gate 1 baseline: 63.7% Pass@1 on legacy syntax. Gate 2 target: &gt;70% on default syntax. <a href="https://github.com/karwalski/toke-model">toke-model</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="timeline-milestone complete">
      <div class="milestone-marker"></div>
      <div class="milestone-content">
        <div class="milestone-header">
          <span class="milestone-id">2.5</span>
          <span class="milestone-title">Gate 2: Default Syntax Compilation</span>
          <span class="phase-status complete">PASS</span>
        </div>
        <p class="milestone-desc"><strong>Gate 2: PASS (2026-05-22).</strong> 100% compilation Pass@1 on 700 benchmark tasks. The corpus was rebuilt from scratch: 25,953 records including 6,069 from the loke production codebase (698 files, 87K lines of working toke). A single canonical system prompt replaced three inconsistent variants. 22 foreign-keyword compiler hints and 6 <code>--migrate</code> transforms were added for common LLM patterns. Functional correctness (correct I/O) is ~8% &mdash; the model mastered syntax but algorithmic reasoning requires execution-verified reinforcement learning, which is the next phase.</p>
        <p class="milestone-technical">Qwen 2.5 Coder 7B + QLoRA (rank 64, alpha 128), 37 hours on NVIDIA A10G. 16K BPE tokenizer trained on normalised v0.3 code achieves 52% token reduction vs cl100k. <a href="https://github.com/karwalski/toke-model">toke-model</a></p>

        <div class="corpus-stage">
          <div class="stage-header"><span class="stage-label">Gate 2 Corpus</span><span class="stage-title">Default Syntax, Verified</span></div>
          <div class="phase-details">
            <div class="phase-stat"><span class="stat-label">Training records</span><span class="stat-value">25,953</span></div>
            <div class="phase-stat"><span class="stat-label">Compilation Pass@1</span><span class="stat-value">100%</span></div>
            <div class="phase-stat"><span class="stat-label">Token reduction</span><span class="stat-value">52% vs cl100k</span></div>
            <div class="phase-stat"><span class="stat-label">Functional Pass@1</span><span class="stat-value">~8% (next target)</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="phase-bar"><div class="phase-bar-fill" style="width:100%"></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="gate-marker">
      <div class="gate-line"></div>
      <div class="gate-content">
        <span class="gate-label">Gate 2 &mdash; PASS</span>
        <span class="gate-criteria">100% compilation Pass@1 &mdash; 7B model outperforms Gate 1 baseline (63.7% &rarr; 100%)</span>
      </div>
      <div class="gate-line"></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- PHASE 3 -->
  <div class="timeline-phase-group">
    <div class="phase-group-header">
      <span class="phase-group-label">Phase 3</span>
      <span class="phase-group-title">Multiple models &amp; self-improvement</span>
    </div>
    <p class="phase-summary">Phase 3 proves the approach works across different AI architectures and builds a self-improvement loop where AI models generate new training data autonomously.</p>
    <p class="phase-technical">Epics 3.1&ndash;3.6. 7B + 32B models. Llama 3.1 family evaluation. Self-improvement: 500 programs/day. ~400 compute-hours total.</p>

    <div class="timeline-milestone complete">
      <div class="milestone-marker"></div>
      <div class="milestone-content">
        <div class="milestone-header">
          <span class="milestone-id">3.1</span>
          <span class="milestone-title">MCP Server &amp; Tooling Protocol</span>
          <span class="phase-status complete">Complete</span>
        </div>
        <p class="milestone-desc">JSON-based tooling protocol server for editor and AI agent integration.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="timeline-milestone complete">
      <div class="milestone-marker"></div>
      <div class="milestone-content">
        <div class="milestone-header">
          <span class="milestone-id">3.2</span>
          <span class="milestone-title">Research Review &amp; Remediation</span>
          <span class="phase-status complete">Complete</span>
        </div>
        <p class="milestone-desc">Comprehensive research review across 8 teams covering compiler hardening, conformance, spec completeness, corpus quality, tokenizer validation, model reproducibility, and security. All findings remediated.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="timeline-milestone complete">
      <div class="milestone-marker"></div>
      <div class="milestone-content">
        <div class="milestone-header">
          <span class="milestone-id">3.3</span>
          <span class="milestone-title">Default Syntax Compiler Implementation</span>
          <span class="phase-status complete">Complete</span>
        </div>
        <p class="milestone-desc">Full compiler support for the 55-character default syntax &mdash; lexer, parser, type checker, and LLVM backend updated. 172 conformance tests passing.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="timeline-milestone in-progress">
      <div class="milestone-marker"></div>
      <div class="milestone-content">
        <div class="milestone-header">
          <span class="milestone-id">3.4</span>
          <span class="milestone-title">Functional Correctness (Gate 3)</span>
          <span class="phase-status in-progress">Next</span>
        </div>
        <p class="milestone-desc">Gate 2 achieved 100% compilation but ~8% functional correctness. Next phase: execution-verified RLVR training with randomised inputs, curriculum learning, and self-improvement loop using the Gate 2 model to generate candidate solutions. Target: &ge;35% functional Pass@1.</p>
        <p class="milestone-technical">Plan: 200K+ execution-verified records via DeepSeek V3.2, GRPO/RLVR with compile+test reward, adaptive curriculum. See <a href="https://github.com/karwalski/toke/blob/main/docs/spec/training-next-phase.md">training-next-phase.md</a> and <a href="https://github.com/karwalski/toke/blob/main/docs/spec/research-feedback-request.md">research feedback request</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="timeline-milestone planned">
      <div class="milestone-marker"></div>
      <div class="milestone-content">
        <div class="milestone-header">
          <span class="milestone-id">3.5</span>
          <span class="milestone-title">Self-Improvement Loop</span>
          <span class="phase-status planned">Planned</span>
        </div>
        <p class="milestone-desc">Autonomous corpus growth: 500 programs/day validated without human initiation.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="timeline-milestone planned">
      <div class="milestone-marker"></div>
      <div class="milestone-content">
        <div class="milestone-header">
          <span class="milestone-id">3.6</span>
          <span class="milestone-title">Multi-Model Evaluation</span>
          <span class="phase-status planned">Planned</span>
        </div>
        <p class="milestone-desc">Llama 3.1 family evaluation (8B, 70B). Cross-family Pass@1 comparison.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="gate-marker">
      <div class="gate-line"></div>
      <div class="gate-content">
        <span class="gate-label">Gate 3</span>
        <span class="gate-criteria">&ge;70% Pass@1 on 2+ model families, self-improvement loop running</span>
      </div>
      <div class="gate-line"></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- PHASE 4 -->
  <div class="timeline-phase-group">
    <div class="phase-group-header">
      <span class="phase-group-label">Phase 4</span>
      <span class="phase-group-title">Standardisation &amp; ecosystem</span>
    </div>
    <p class="phase-summary">The final phase formalises toke into a publishable standard with a full conformance suite, package ecosystem, and governance structure.</p>
    <p class="phase-technical">Epics 4.1&ndash;4.5. Complete EBNF + formal semantics. 900+ conformance tests. LSP stub, package registry. Consortium proposal.</p>

    <div class="timeline-milestone complete">
      <div class="milestone-marker"></div>
      <div class="milestone-content">
        <div class="milestone-header">
          <span class="milestone-id">4.1</span>
          <span class="milestone-title">Complete Language Specification</span>
          <span class="phase-status complete">Complete</span>
        </div>
        <p class="milestone-desc">Full formal specification published &mdash; EBNF grammar, static semantics, runtime contract, memory model, error code registry, and machine-readable Tree-sitter grammar.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="timeline-milestone complete">
      <div class="milestone-marker"></div>
      <div class="milestone-content">
        <div class="milestone-header">
          <span class="milestone-id">4.2</span>
          <span class="milestone-title">Conformance Suite</span>
          <span class="phase-status complete">Complete</span>
        </div>
        <p class="milestone-desc">600+ conformance tests covering lexical, grammar, type/semantic, and diagnostic schema validation.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="timeline-milestone planned">
      <div class="milestone-marker"></div>
      <div class="milestone-content">
        <div class="milestone-header">
          <span class="milestone-id">4.3&ndash;4.4</span>
          <span class="milestone-title">Tooling &amp; Self-Redesign</span>
          <span class="phase-status planned">Planned</span>
        </div>
        <p class="milestone-desc">LSP editor integration, package registry, and a self-redesign pilot where AI proposes language improvements.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="timeline-milestone planned">
      <div class="milestone-marker"></div>
      <div class="milestone-content">
        <div class="milestone-header">
          <span class="milestone-id">4.5</span>
          <span class="milestone-title">Consortium &amp; Adoption</span>
          <span class="phase-status planned">Planned</span>
        </div>
        <p class="milestone-desc">Governance document, versioning, change process. Consortium proposal for standardisation and enterprise adoption.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="gate-marker">
      <div class="gate-line"></div>
      <div class="gate-content">
        <span class="gate-label">Gate 4</span>
        <span class="gate-criteria">All benchmarks met, spec complete, consortium proposal ready</span>
      </div>
      <div class="gate-line"></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- PHASE 5 -->
  <div class="timeline-phase-group">
    <div class="phase-group-header">
      <span class="phase-group-label">Phase 5</span>
      <span class="phase-group-title">1B purpose-built model</span>
    </div>
    <p class="phase-summary">Phase 5 replaces the fine-tuning approach with a 1B parameter model trained from scratch on toke programs. A smaller model purpose-built for toke is expected to outperform larger fine-tuned models on toke-specific code generation, because it learns toke as a native language rather than adapting from Python or C.</p>
    <p class="phase-technical">Architecture design, corpus preparation (comment-free, 55-char default syntax), training infrastructure, full training run, and evaluation against fine-tuned 7B baseline.</p>

    <div class="timeline-milestone planned">
      <div class="milestone-marker"></div>
      <div class="milestone-content">
        <div class="milestone-header">
          <span class="milestone-id">5.1</span>
          <span class="milestone-title">1B Model Architecture Design</span>
          <span class="phase-status planned">Planned</span>
        </div>
        <p class="milestone-desc">Design a 1B parameter transformer architecture optimised for toke code generation. Evaluate decoder-only vs encoder-decoder, context length, and attention patterns suited to toke's compact syntax.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="timeline-milestone planned">
      <div class="milestone-marker"></div>
      <div class="milestone-content">
        <div class="milestone-header">
          <span class="milestone-id">5.2</span>
          <span class="milestone-title">Training Corpus Preparation</span>
          <span class="phase-status planned">Planned</span>
        </div>
        <p class="milestone-desc">Prepare the from-scratch training corpus: comment-free, 55-character default syntax, matched to the purpose-built tokenizer. Includes deduplication, quality filtering, and curriculum ordering.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="timeline-milestone planned">
      <div class="milestone-marker"></div>
      <div class="milestone-content">
        <div class="milestone-header">
          <span class="milestone-id">5.3</span>
          <span class="milestone-title">Training Infrastructure</span>
          <span class="phase-status planned">Planned</span>
        </div>
        <p class="milestone-desc">Set up training infrastructure for a full from-scratch training run &mdash; hardware provisioning, distributed training framework, checkpointing, and monitoring.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="timeline-milestone planned">
      <div class="milestone-marker"></div>
      <div class="milestone-content">
        <div class="milestone-header">
          <span class="milestone-id">5.4</span>
          <span class="milestone-title">1B Model Training</span>
          <span class="phase-status planned">Planned</span>
        </div>
        <p class="milestone-desc">Train the 1B parameter model from scratch on the toke corpus. Multiple training runs with hyperparameter search. Target: the model learns toke as its native language.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="timeline-milestone planned">
      <div class="milestone-marker"></div>
      <div class="milestone-content">
        <div class="milestone-header">
          <span class="milestone-id">5.5</span>
          <span class="milestone-title">1B Model Evaluation</span>
          <span class="phase-status planned">Planned</span>
        </div>
        <p class="milestone-desc">Evaluate the 1B purpose-built model against the fine-tuned 7B baseline on toke code generation benchmarks. Target: 1B purpose-built outperforms 7B fine-tuned on Pass@1, compilation rate, and token efficiency.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="gate-marker">
      <div class="gate-line"></div>
      <div class="gate-content">
        <span class="gate-label">Gate 5</span>
        <span class="gate-criteria">1B purpose-built model outperforms fine-tuned 7B on toke generation benchmarks</span>
      </div>
      <div class="gate-line"></div>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>

<!-- ================================================================== -->
<!-- Built with toke                                                    -->
<!-- ================================================================== -->

<div class="built-with">
  <h2>Built with toke</h2>
  <div class="built-card">
    <h3>ooke &mdash; CMS and Web Framework</h3>
    <p>This website is built and served by <a href="/ooke">ooke</a> &mdash; toke's own CMS and web framework. File-system routing, flat-file Markdown content, a template engine, and a native HTTP server. No Node.js, no Python, no nginx. One compiled binary serves every page you are reading.</p>
    <a href="/ooke">Explore ooke &rarr;</a>
  </div>
  <div class="built-card">
    <h3>loke &mdash; Local Intelligence Layer</h3>
    <p>A locally-run intelligence layer that sits between users, their data, and external LLMs &mdash; minimising token spend, maximising privacy, and keeping sensitive data where it belongs: on your device.</p>
    <p>The market has split into enterprise cloud gateways that need DevOps expertise, local model runners that don't optimise cloud-bound traffic, and multi-provider chat UIs that pass prompts through unchanged. loke occupies the empty quadrant at the centre &mdash; privacy, optimisation, and routing in one place, running locally.</p>
    <a href="/loke">Explore loke &rarr;</a>
  </div>
</div>

