        <p style="font-size:0.85rem;color:#aaa;margin-bottom:0.8rem;">Use the REST API directly or connect via MCP (Model Context Protocol) from Claude Code, Cursor, Codex, or any MCP-compatible client.</p>
        <pre style="background:#0d0d0d;padding:0.8rem;border-radius:4px;font-size:0.75rem;overflow-x:auto;color:#82e0aa;margin-bottom:1rem;">curl -X POST api.tokelang.dev/v1/generate \
  -H "X-Api-Key: YOUR_KEY" \
  -d '{"description": "Sum an array"}'

{"source": "m=sum;f=sum(arr:@i64)...",
 "tokens_in": 159,
 "tokens_out": 28,
 "toke_bpe_out": 13}</pre>
        <p style="font-size:0.8rem;color:#888;">The response includes three token counts: model input, model output (Qwen tokenizer), and the same output measured by toke's purpose-built BPE &mdash; showing the 52% efficiency gain a toke-native model would achieve.</p>
